-- title:
--   Invertibility of the component ideal sheaves over O
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A\to L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ that is an $A$-algebra, and write $X=\mathrm{TwoChart.modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ for the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, with base change $X_k=X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}k$. Assume given two schemes $C_1,C_2$ proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral and integral over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, together with closed immersions $i_\nu:C_\nu\to X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k$ whose images cover all points of $X_k$, such that $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced with $\operatorname{card}=n>0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O:A\to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa:O\to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ the structure map $A\to k$; let $bc:X_k\to X_O:=X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}O$ be a morphism commuting with the first projections and with the second projections up to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Then the kernel ideal sheaves of the composites $bc\circ i_1$ and $bc\circ i_2$ are both invertible in the sense of the project predicate `IsInvertible`: around every point of $X_O$ there is an affine open $U$ and $f\in\Gamma(X_O,U)$ with the point in the basic open of $f$, such that on the affine basic open of $f$ the ideal is generated by a single non-zero-divisor.
--
--   The two components of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$, viewed inside the model over the unramified extension $O$, are effective Cartier divisors: the classical statement that vertical prime divisors on a regular arithmetic surface are locally principal. It feeds the intersection-theoretic computations on this model, namely the Euler-characteristic computation for the powers and inverses of these ideal sheaves and the statement that the product of the two component ideals is the ideal of the whole special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isInvertible_ker_comp_baseChange_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

